```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .joke-container {
            border: 2px solid blue;
            padding: 20px;
            width: 300px;
            text-align: center;
            color: blue;
        }
        .joke-container h1 {
            color: black;
        }
        .joke-container p {
            font-style: italic;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <p id="joke">[Funny Joke]</p>
        <button onclick="revealPunchline()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealPunchline() {
            const jokeElement = document.getElementById('joke');
            jokeElement.textContent = "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!";
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a basic webpage with a centered container that holds the joke. The joke is initially hidden and revealed when the button is clicked. You can replace the joke text with your own or dynamically load it from an API if needed.
